+In level time (sites with `x_1 + x_2 + x_3 = t`) the three-dimensional monotone formation law is a synchronous probabilistic cellular automaton on `Z^2` with the north-east-center neighborhood, well defined at every coupling, whose stationary two-sided chains are exactly the translation-invariant `Z^3` laws (S0). Its kernel is the rule's three-neighbor conditional, computed in closed form: unanimous `p³/(p³+q³+4r³)`, orthogonal `2:1` `p²r/V_3`, antipodal `2:1` `p²q/(pq(p+q)+4r³)`, tie `p/(3(p+q))`; every deviation from the majority is `O(1/p)`, and the majority is the most likely output iff `p > max(q, r)` (S1). The noiseless limit is a majority rule that is an eroder: a finite island of a binary coarse-graining dies within `M_1 + M_2 + M_3 − t_0 + 1` levels, by the monotonicity of the three coordinate maxima (S2). The coarse-graining "not `a`" is dominated site by site by the majority automaton with independent noise `ε(p) = max(q, r)/p + O(p^{−2})`, an exact rational (`35/44, 21/71, 71/971, 211/10211, 2011/1002011` at `(p,1,2)`, `p = 3, 10, 30, 100, 1000`), the maximum switching from the antipodal to the orthogonal `2:1` triple between `p = 10` and `p = 30` (S3). Every finite cross-section has a unique stationary plane law, but as `p → ∞` the six constant planes become absorbing and the second eigenvalue tends to one: on the `2×2` cross-section the memory of the starting constant plane after eight steps rises from `3·10^{−6}` at `p = 3` to `0.549` at `p = 100`, while the orbit quotient (the six constant planes identified) contracts at every coupling — fast collapse onto an ordered plane, slow forgetting of which (S4). In two dimensions the law is unique at every coupling, its rows are `K`-chains with eigenvalue `(p − q)/Z_1 < 1`, and the two-predecessor limit has no majority: no ordered phase at any coupling (S5). The ordered phase in three dimensions is stated as one exact obligation — the stability of the dominating noisy eroder below a threshold `ε_0`, which by S3 would give at least six extremal invariant laws — with the classical theorem named as a reference and not used, and the block's own contour attempt recorded with its obstruction (the naive explanation tree's size is not linear in the number of noise sites) (S6).
